How can I use Java code to transform a given sentence into active voice using Markdown?
Here's an example Java code snippet that can achieve this:
String sentence = "[Active voice] The woman drove the car.";
String[] words = sentence.split(" ");
String subject = "";
String verb = "";
String object = "";
String output = "";
for (String word : words) {
    if (word.equals("The")) {
        subject = "The woman";
    } else if (word.equals("drove")) {
        verb = "drove";
    } else if (word.equals("car.")) {
        object = "the car.";
    }
}
output = subject + " " + verb + " " + object;
output = output.replace("[Active voice]", "");
System.out.println(output);
This code will output "The woman drove the car." in active voice.

