What is the Python code to calculate the sum of the x-coordinates of all points on the surface of a sphere with a radius of 5 units, given a set of three-dimensional coordinates that lie within the range of -10 to 10 on all axes and only include points that have a radius of exactly 5 units? Here is the C# code that can help solve this problem:
double sumX = 0.0;
for (int x = -10; x <= 10; x++)
{
    for (int y = -10; y <= 10; y++)
    {
        for (int z = -10; z <= 10; z++)
        {
            double radius = Math.Sqrt(x * x + y * y + z * z);
            if (radius == 5.0)
            {
                sumX += x;
            }
        }
    }
}
