Suppose we have an image file in PNG format containing a color wheel, which displays all possible color combinations. If we choose red and green from the list of colors [red, green, blue], what would be their color wheel combination?
Assuming the PNG image file is named "color_wheel.png" and contains all possible color combinations, we can use MATLAB code to display the image and find the color combination of red and green. 
First, we read the image file using the imread() function:
im = imread('color_wheel.png');
Then, we can display the image using imshow():
imshow(im);
To find the color combination of red and green, we can look for the point where the red and green colors intersect on the color wheel. This can be done using the ginput() function to obtain the coordinates of the point on the image:
[x,y] = ginput(1);
The coordinates of the point will correspond to a specific color combination on the color wheel. We can use the impixel() function to get the RGB values of the pixel at the chosen coordinates:
rgb = impixel(im,x,y);
The RGB values will give us an idea of what the color combination of red and green would look like on the color wheel.

